@{
    NopHtml.AddTitleParts("Airless Paint Sprayer Repair");
    NopHtml.AddMetaDescriptionParts("Airless paint sprayer repair, service department, Portland OR. Authorized warranty repair center for many airless brands like Graco.");
    NopHtml.AddMetaKeywordParts("Graco, airless, paint, sprayer, repair, pump, rebuild, fix, sprayers, repairing, parts, cleaning, authorized, warranty");
}

<h1 class="h2 margin-block-end-4">Airless Paint Sprayer Repair &amp; Service</h1>
<div class="row">
	<div class="col-md-4">
		<div class="card">
			<span class="fw-bold h4">Also see</span>
			<ul class="list-unstyled">
				<li><a href=@Url.Action("Maintenance", "Airless")>Airless Maintenance</a></li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</div>
	<div class="flow">
		<h3>Warranty Service</h3>
		<p>If you would like us to repair your airless paint sprayer under warranty;</p>
		<p>Bring it in to us at the address below, during regular business hours, along with a copy of your receipt showing your purchase of the sprayer.</p>
		<p>Or, if you ship the sprayer to us please follow the directions below.</p>
		<h4>Shipment of Your Airless Sprayer for Warranty Repair</h4>
		<p>First call our repair dept., 866-208-6087, for a Repair Authorization. We will also need a copy of the invoice that lists the unit to be repaired in order to file a warranty claim.</p>
		<p>
			Then you would need to send it insured and shipping paid with the RA# on the
			outside of the box along with a copy of your receipt/invoice, your full name address and
			telephone number to;
			<br>Portland Compressor<br>ATTN: Repair<br>7440 SW Bonita Rd <br>Portland OR 97224
		</p>
		<p>Once received we would inspect it, diagnose it...</p>
		<p>
			If it is a problem covered by warranty we would get the required parts to fix it if
			we don't have them here, then repair it and send it back freight paid and insured
			(depending on the manufacturers warranty policies, most pay shipping back to you).
		</p>
		<p>
			If it is a problem not covered by warranty we would contact you about what it would
			cost to fix it, then fix it if that is what you want to do and ship it back insured at
			your expense. There is a $80.00 diagnostic fee for non-warranty work. This fee is credited
			to your repair bill if you choose to repair or can be applied to the purchase of a new
			airless sprayer.
		</p>
		<h3><a name="General_Repair">General Repair</a></h3>
		<p>If you would like us to repair your sprayer NOT covered under warranty.</p>
		<p>Bring it in to us at the address below, during regular business hours.</p>
		<h4>Shipment of Your Airless Sprayer for NON-warranty Repair</h4>
		<p>First call our repair dept., 866-208-6087, for a Repair Authorization.</p>
		<p>
			There is a $80 charge that must be paid upfront, BEFORE any work will be done. This
			$80 charge will then be credited towards the first hour of labor.<br><br>Then you would
			need to send it insured and shipping paid with the RA# on the outside of the box along
			with a copy of your receipt/invoice, your full name address and telephone # to;
			<br>Portland
			Compressor<br>ATTN: Repair<br>7440 SW Bonita Rd <br>Portland OR 97224
		</p>
		<p>Once received we would inspect it, diagnose it...</p>
		<p>
			Upon the estimate, we will repair the machine. You would be responsible for any shipping
			costs in returning the sprayer. Our shop charge is $80 an hour, in addition to any parts
			that may be needed to repair the machine.
		</p>
	</div>
</div>